messages:
rachel: starting a small docs PR to add a Node quickstart for Optimize toolkit (continuous batching + cache + quant fallback). need a reviewer and a runnable snippet. @tom @nikhil
 tom: keep it <20 lines, Node/browser pattern, mention quant_profile for low-latency apps.
nikhil: add a docs-ci job to run snippet with a mock server so we catch runtime regressions. also watch TOC anchors (they moved recently).
amanda: include one-line guidance on when NOT to use continuous batching (very low QPS single-request apps).
rachel: first draft snippet below - copy/pasteable Node SDK v0.8:
```javascript
// Node SDK v0.8 - continuous batching + cache + quant fallback
const { RedwoodClient } = require('@redwood/inference');
const client = new RedwoodClient();
(async () => {
  const res = await client.generate({
    model: 'optimize/interactive-v1',
    input: 'Summarize recent messages',
    batching: { mode: 'continuous', batch_window_ms: 20, max_batch_tokens: 800 },
    cache: { enable_prefix_kv: true, ttl_seconds: 300 },
    quant_profile: 'latency-8bit',
    fallback: { on_high_contention: { quant_profile: 'compact-5bit' } }
  });
  console.log(res.text);
})();
```
nikhil: looks good. i'll draft .github workflow to run this with REDWOOD_API_KEY=ci-mock and a mocked endpoint.
tom: add warmup note: prefill a short prompt to warm KV cache for long threads. also call out minor token differences with 5bit profiles.
amanda: reviewed wording, clarified the "when not to use" sentence.
